### Rust ###
# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information

# End of https://www.toptal.com/developers/gitignore/api/rust

# Demo artifacts. The recording is tracked: it is the source of truth for
# re-exporting the demo, and cargo already keeps the whole directory out of the
# published crate via `exclude = ["demo/"]` in Cargo.toml — so crates.io is not
# a reason to hide it from git. The rendered output is not tracked: this demo's
# gif is ~36 MB (a TUI that redraws every frame compresses badly), and the
# landing serves the mp4 at public/demos/canopy.mp4.
demo/dist/
